        text: ["**0**: the job is done. **75**: the machine is unfit (the swap or memory guard stopped a story). dbench waits 5 minutes and tries again without counting a restart; `run.sh` itself refuses to go on until the machine has recovered. **3**: a resource is missing (a browser, say); every later story would hit the same wall, so the job fails at once.", "**Anything else** is a crash: the job goes to the front of the queue after 30 s and resumes at the first unfinished story, up to 3 times. The same failure twice with no progress (a broken checkout, a server that exits at start) fails the job at once instead of using every restart. If the server itself restarts mid-job it adopts the running harness; if the harness is gone, it requeues the job."],
